{
  "Esther.4.7.18-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 15 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Esther 4:7.18</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Esther 4:7.18</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir yod)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/15-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is in the left margin; it is a yatir yod. The word has 3 yods; the first is vowelized and accented. Neither the second or third yod is vowelized or accented; the second yod in the word will be noted as a yatir here.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere has a single unvowelized, unaccented yod before the final mem.\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBHLA has no entry for this verse.\n\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-15\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-15</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Esther.5.14.22-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2021.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2021.08.07, number: 19 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Esther 5:14.22</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Esther 5:14.22</h1>\n  <h2>Word lacks accent, add note 'c'; MAM ends the word with a Maqaf (  ס־  ).</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes/images/2021.08.07/19-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Ben Denckla</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes.xml?2021.08.07-19\">2021.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2021.08.07-19</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Esther.7.8.10-t.html": "<html>\n<header profile=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/11/profile\" > \n        <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/> \n        <title>Esther 7:8.10</title>\n</header>\n    \n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n        <h1>Esther 7:8.10</h1>\n        <h4>Based on color photos, a revia instead of a zaqef qatan is uncertain.</h4>\n        \n        <table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5pt\"><tr><td>\n            <center>\n                <img src=\"../../Changes/2021.04.01 - Changes/images/2021.02.22/26-Detail.jpg\" border=\"4pt\"/>\n            </center>\n        </td></tr>\n        <p/>\n        <tr><td>\n            <center><i>Credit: Sefaria.org.\n            </i></center>\n        </td></tr>\n        </table>\n        <p/>\n            Two dots over the pe might be taken as revias. \n            One is almost touching the top of the pe, the other is above the gap between the pe and the lamed.\n            The revia on top of the pe is small and faint. \n            Compare with the revias in 7:7.10 immediately above it or in the same verse at 7:8.24.\n       <p/>\n          The upper dot of the zaqaf qatan might be considered hidden by the munah in 7:7.6 immediately above it.\n       <p/>\n          The JPS Tanakh has a zaqef qatan.\n          <br/>\n          The \"Miqra according to Masora\" shows a revia. \n         <p/>\n        <b><i>Steven Salisbury</i></b>\n        <p align=\"right\"><b>2021.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2021.02.22-26</b></p>\n        <p/>\n        <table border=\"1pt\" align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"16pt\">\n            <tr><td>\n              <span style=\"color:blue;font-size:14pt\">\n                  <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a>\n              </span>\n              <p/>\n              <span style=\"color:blue;font-size:14pt\">\n                  <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n              </span>\n            </td?</tr>\n        </table>\n        <p/>\n        </body>\n</html>\n",
  "Esther.9.27.3-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.15, number: 37 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Esther 9:27.3</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Esther 9:27.3</h1>\n  <h2>Remove unsupported dagesh from last vav; place a qubuts under lamed in qere word. Add note 'q'. [וְקִבְּל֣וּ]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.15/37-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The qere in the right margin ends in a vav that is not present in the ketiv body text. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tThe ketiv body text has a qubuts then munah under the lamed; no dagesh is available for the final vav. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tThe UXLC retains the qubuts on the lamed to be true to the LC image. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tA transcription note 'q' is added to emphasize this decision.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh (acting as a shuruq dot) in the final vav in the qere word, וְקִבְּל֣וּ.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.15-37\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.15-37</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>"
}
